mapping "e250.1" source="e250" target="SNOMED_CT:102412001" relationship=related_to {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source e250 SNOMED CT 102412001 = ICF environmental factor: sound (the acoustic environment as
        determinant of functioning, e2 Natural environment chapter). Target = (sctid 102412001, active).
        The SNOMED CT concept names a corresponding acoustic environmental referent, but is framed as a
        clinical event of pollution rather than a functioning-determinant; relationship is loose
        association, not identity/subsumption. Per standards related-vs-no_match boundary: a real,
        defensible environmental-clinical link exists, so record as related at (weak) rather than
        discard. Mapping-type=related (target clinically associated but on a different ontological
        axis).
        """
}
mapping "e2500.1" source="e2500" target="SNOMED_CT:250888003" relationship=related_to {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source e2500 SNOMED CT 250888003 = ICF environmental factor: sound intensity/volume (e250
        sub-block). Target = (sctid 250888003, active). The SNOMED CT concept is the directly corresponding
        real-world observable for sound intensity; it is framed as a measurable observable rather than a
        functioning-determinant. Defensible related link at (weak): same physical referent, different
        ontological axis. mapping_type=related.
        """
}
assessment "e2501.omop" source="e2501" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
assessment "e2508.omop" source="e2508" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
assessment "e2509.omop" source="e2509" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
mapping "e255.1" source="e255" target="SNOMED_CT:735932007" relationship=related_to {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source e255 SNOMED CT 735932007 = ICF environmental factor: vibration (e2 Natural environment
        chapter). Target = (sctid 735932007, active). The SNOMED CT concept names the same physical
        environmental referent (vibration as exposure), but is scoped to occupational exposure (a
        narrower framing) and modeled as a clinical event rather than a functioning-determinant.
        Defensible related link at (weak): same physical referent, different axis and framing.
        mapping_type=related.
        """
}
mapping "e260.1" source="e260" target="SNOMED_CT:102413006" relationship=related_to {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source e260 SNOMED CT 102413006 = ICF environmental factor: air quality (e2 Natural environment
        chapter). Target = (sctid 102413006, active). The SNOMED CT concept is the directly corresponding
        air-environment referent, but is framed as a pollution event (a negative/quality-degraded state)
        rather than the neutral functioning-determinant (which can be a facilitator or barrier).
        Defensible related link at (weak): same environmental axis, different framing.
        mapping_type=related.
        """
}
