mapping "e320.1" source="e320" target="SNOMED_CT:113163005" relationship=related_to {
    confidence 1 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence-unassessable@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source e320 SNOMED CT 113163005 = ICF environmental factor: support from friends (e3 chapter).
        Target = (sctid 113163005, active). The SNOMED CT concept names the corresponding social referent
        (friend) but is a person/relationship record, not a support-as-functioning-determinant; the
        source is about the support relationship, the target is the person role. Defensible related link
        at (weak) per the related-vs-no_match boundary (a real social-clinical association exists,
        analogous to the Z800 family-history pattern). mapping_type=related.
        """
}
mapping "e325.1" source="e325" target="SNOMED_CT:48385004" relationship=related_to {
    confidence 1 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence-unassessable@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source e325 SNOMED CT 48385004 = ICF environmental factor: support from acquaintances, peers,
        colleagues, neighbours and community members (e3 chapter). Target = (sctid 48385004, active).
        The SNOMED CT concept names one social-referent role within this broad source grouping
        (acquaintance), not the support relationship itself; source is about support, target is a person
        role. Heterogeneous source (five roles) and only one role has a direct SNOMED CT person concept, so
        a single partial/related target is weak but defensible as a lead. mapping_type=related at
        (weak).
        """
}
assessment "e330.omop" source="e330" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
assessment "e335.omop" source="e335" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
mapping "e340.1" source="e340" target="SNOMED_CT:133932002" relationship=related_to {
    confidence 1 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence-unassessable@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source e340 SNOMED CT 133932002 158881006 = ICF environmental factor: support from personal care
        providers and personal assistants (e3 chapter). Targets: SNOMED CT 133932002 = and SNOMED CT 158881006
        = (both active). The SNOMED CT concepts name the corresponding caregiver/assistant roles, but are
        person/occupation records, not a support-as-functioning-determinant; the source is about the
        support relationship, the targets are the roles. Each target covers one facet of the two-part
        source (caregiver facet, assistant facet); recorded as two related links (strongest-first) at
        (weak) per the multi-target rule and related-vs-no_match boundary. mapping_type=related for
        both.
        """
}
mapping "e340.2" source="e340" target="SNOMED_CT:158881006" relationship=related_to {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
}
assessment "e345.omop" source="e345" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
assessment "e350.omop" source="e350" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
mapping "e355.1" source="e355" target="SNOMED_CT:223366009" relationship=related_to {
    confidence 1 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence-unassessable@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source e355 = ICF environmental factor SNOMED CT 223366009 (Stöd från yrkesutövare inom hälso- och
        sjukvård) — a contextual determinant. Target (person concept). Why this target: it is the only
        SNOMED CT concept identifying the *category of person* the source describes as the support
        provider; no SNOMED CT concept represents. Why : the source is an ICF environmental factor, not a
        person or finding — the link is a loose clinical association (related), recorded as a lead for
        reviewers, not an identity. Semantic mismatch (contextual factor vs person) caps confidence at
        weak.
        """
}
assessment "e360.omop" source="e360" outcome=no_match target-system="OMOP_EXT"
mapping "e398.1" source="e398" target="SNOMED_CT:445051000124100" relationship=related_to {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source e398 = ICF environmental-factor chapter-e3 residual SNOMED CT 445051000124100 (andra
        specificerade). Target. Why this target: it is the closest SNOMED CT concept to the ICF
        personal/social-support idea; it is a *status/finding about* social support, not the
        environmental factor itself. Why : source is an ICF contextual factor and a residual bucket —
        loose related link, recorded as a reviewer lead, not an identity. No exact or broader target
        exists because the ICF factor semantics are absent in SNOMED CT.
        """
}
mapping "e398A.1" source="e398A" target="SNOMED_CT:365498000" relationship=related_to {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source e398A = Swedish ICF-extension environmental factor SNOMED CT 365498000 (Personligt stöd från
        person som vårdar eller stödjer en närstående) — i.e. support from an informal carer. Target.
        Why this target: it is the only SNOMED CT concept directly about support for/from informal
        caregivers; it is a *finding about* support availability, not the ICF environmental factor
        itself. Why : contextual-factor vs finding semantic mismatch; related link recorded as a
        reviewer lead, not identity. Defensible association, but weak.
        """
}
mapping "e399.1" source="e399" target="SNOMED_CT:445051000124100" relationship=related_to {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source e399 = ICF environmental-factor chapter-e3 SNOMED CT 445051000124100 (ospecificerade).
        Target. Why this target: closest SNOMED CT concept to the broad personal/social-support idea, but
        it is a status/finding-about, not the environmental factor. Why : source is an unspecified ICF
        contextual factor — loose related link for reviewer follow-up, not an identity; the unspecified
        framing plus the semantic mismatch cap confidence at weak.
        """
}
